# Manifest of the examples shown in the web interface's gallery, read by
# src/06-user-interface/web/gen_examples/gen_examples.ml to generate the
# module Examples_tpe (see src/06-user-interface/web/dune).
#
# One example per non-blank, non-comment line, five fields separated by ' | ':
#
#   group | title | grade | path | description
#
# - group: the heading of the gallery section the example is listed under.
# - title: the heading of the example's card, without a prefix already given
#   by the group.
# - grade: the grading monoid the web interface switches to when the example
#   is loaded (a key of Grades.GradeRegistry.grade_modules).
# - path: the example's file, relative to this directory.
# - description: one sentence, shown on the example's card.
#
# Each group is summarised by one line of four fields, the first the word
# 'group', placed before the group's examples:
#
#   group | label | short | summary
#
# - label: the group, as its examples name it.
# - short: the label's short form, shown with the title of the example last
#   loaded on the button that opens the gallery; distinct for distinct groups.
# - summary: one line, shown beside the group's heading.
#
# A group without a summary, or a summary without examples, is an error.
#
# Examples are listed in the order they appear in the gallery: groups in the
# order given here, and within a group from the simplest example to the most
# advanced.

group | Effect handlers | Handlers | Operations handled by clauses that respect their grades.
Effect handlers | Lower bounds | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_lower_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation once it has waited for at least the operation's grade.
Effect handlers | Upper bounds | time-upper-bound | handlers/handlers_upper_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation at any point up to the operation's grade, or not at all.
Effect handlers | Nested | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_nested.tpe | Nested handlers each resume their own continuation, quantifying over one rigid effect per level of nesting.
Effect handlers | Nested (rejected) | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_nested_reject.tpe | The nested-handlers example with one inner continuation left unresumed, correctly rejected.

group | Time grades | Time | Boxes usable before or within a number of time steps, whole or fractional.
Time grades | Upper bounds | time-upper-bound | time/time_upper.tpe | A box may be unboxed at any point up to its upper-bound grade.
Time grades | Intervals | time-interval | time/time_intervals.tpe | A box grade pairs a lower and an upper time bound, unboxable only within that interval.
Time grades | Intervals (rational) | time-interval-rational | time/rational_time_intervals.tpe | A medication schedule in hours, whose doses and reports are due within intervals with fractional endpoints.

group | Traces | Traces | Finite sets of timed runs of operations, in whole or fractional time.
Traces | Lower bounds | traces-lower-bound | traces/traces_lower.tpe | A 3D-printing pipeline whose operations must be covered by the runs a box demands, waiting banking towards them.
Traces | Upper bounds | traces-upper-bound | traces/traces_upper.tpe | The same pipeline under the allowance order, where a delay pays for operations at their upper runtime bound.
Traces | Intervals | traces-interval | traces/traces_intervals.tpe | The pipeline graded by a pair of a coverage and an allowance bound, compared componentwise.
Traces | Intervals (rational) | traces-interval-rational | traces/rational_traces_intervals.tpe | A weather station timed in seconds, whose operations declare fractional runtime bounds and whose windows are traces with fractional delays.

group | Regular expressions | Regex | Regular languages of runs of operations and ticks.
Regular expressions | Upper bounds | regex-upper-bound-symbolic | regular/regular_traces.tpe | A file-session and an authentication protocol, each graded by a regular language of operations and ticks.

group | Regular expressions with costs | Regex (costs) | Regular runs, operations costing their declared runtimes.
Regular expressions with costs | Lower bounds | regex-cost-lower-bound-symbolic | regular_costs/regular_costs_lower.tpe | A coating line graded by regular lower bounds whose ticks are banked by operations at their lower runtime bounds.
Regular expressions with costs | Upper bounds | regex-cost-upper-bound-symbolic | regular_costs/regular_costs_upper.tpe | A sensor station graded by regular upper bounds whose ticks pay for operations at their upper runtime bounds.
Regular expressions with costs | Intervals | regex-cost-interval-symbolic | regular_costs/regular_costs_intervals.tpe | The coating line graded by pairs of a regular lower and a regular upper bound, compared componentwise.

group | Security levels | Security | Levels touched, alone or with time bounds and outputs.
Security levels | Levels | security-levels | levels/security_levels.tpe | A box at a security level is out of reach once a higher level has been touched since boxing.
Security levels | Embargoes | time-lower-bound-levels | levels/time_lower_levels.tpe | A box paired with a time lower bound and a level: an embargo with a taint check.
Security levels | Expiring capabilities | time-upper-bound-levels | levels/time_upper_levels.tpe | A box paired with a time upper bound and a level: a capability that expires and can be revoked by a taint.
Security levels | Flow-sensitive outputs | flow-levels | levels/flow_levels.tpe | A report whose public post must come before the vault is read, each output graded by the level touched before it.

group | Semidirect products | Semidirect | Grades whose second component is shifted by the first.
Semidirect products | Peak usage | peak-usage | semidirect/peak_usage.tpe | File copies, uploads and log rotations graded by the trough, the net change and the peak of the files and connections they hold.
Semidirect products | Time windows | time-windows | semidirect/time_windows.tpe | A sensor node whose transmissions are graded by the ticks of its frames at which they happen.
Semidirect products | Mode costs | mode-costs | semidirect/mode_costs.tpe | A sensor node whose energy costs depend on whether its radio is on, as max-plus matrices over the modes.

group | Operation counts | Counts | How often each operation is called.
Operation counts | Upper bounds | counts-upper-bound | counts/rate_limits.tpe | A client whose logins and requests are checked against rate limits on each operation.

group | Case studies | Case studies | Larger programs using many features together.
Case studies | 3D printing: time bounds | time-lower-bound | 3dprint/3dprint.tpe | The stages of a 3D print, boxed at the lower time bounds each stage demands.
Case studies | 3D printing: with effect handlers | time-lower-bound | 3dprint/3dprint_handlers.tpe | The same pipeline with each stage an operation, handled by clauses that respect its timing.
Case studies | 3D printing: with trace grades | traces-interval | 3dprint/3dprint_traces.tpe | The same pipeline graded by the traces of operations it may exhibit, bounds on runtime included.
Case studies | Staged release | time-lower-bound-levels | rollout/rollout.tpe | A release deployed in stages, each stage unboxing its approval only after the deployed hosts have been observed and only if nothing untrusted has been touched since the approval, with probes repeated within a budget and hotfixes fetched at the level High.
Case studies | Mail session | regex-cost-upper-bound-symbolic | sessions/mail_session.tpe | A mail session whose retrieval and flagging loops are graded by starred runs, with operations costing their declared runtimes.
